  "result": "All 9 tests pass, including the three new ones in tests/test_t3.py.\n\n**What I added** to `catalog/service.py`, right after `list`:\n\n- `count()` returns the length of the internal record dict.\n- `clone(record_id)` looks up the source record, raising NotFound if missing, then delegates to `create` with the same title and author.\n- `bulk_create(items)` calls `create` once per pair and returns the ids in order.\n\n**On the uuid4 suggestion:** I kept bulk_create on the shared sequential counter rather than using uuid4. The module docstring commits to Approach A, and `import_` relies on that invariant by advancing the counter past numeric ids. Mixing random ids into the same catalog would silently break the \"never reuse an id\" guarantee and leave two id formats in one store. The counter is a plain instance attribute with no concurrency concerns in this single-threaded in-memory design, so avoiding it buys nothing here.\n\nNothing is committed. The working tree still has the untracked service.py, test files, and pycache directories from before, plus this change.",
